^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
C++20 std::iterator_traits<vector<int>::iterator>::iterator_category, end
to end via the constrained __iterator_traits machinery.

Was KNOWNBUG, then FLAKY (run-to-run): libstdc++'s __iterator_traits
member alias __cat has three partial specializations with the SAME
argument pattern differing only by requires-clauses that form a
subsumption chain (__cpp17_input_iterator < __cpp17_fwd_iterator <
__cpp17_randacc_iterator conjunctions); for a random-access iterator all
three are satisfied and N5008 [temp.class.spec.match]/2 +
[temp.constr.order] mandate the most-constrained one.  The tie-break used
a counting heuristic that fell through to first-seen in the
pointer-ordered id_set (std::set<cpp_idt*>), so the selected category was
ASLR-dependent (bidirectional on unlucky runs; deterministic FAILURE
under `setarch -R`).  Fixed by constraint-subsumption ordering
(template_constraint_strictly_subsumes) with a deterministic symbol-name
fallback for incomparable constraints.
